var e=[{id:`memory`,name:`Cities & Memory`,index:0,color:`#d8a657`,blurb:`Five cities in which remembering is the architecture: an evening that feels already lived, a dream reached too late, a past stored in measurements, a city frozen into a mnemonic until it vanishes, a postcard of a place that was never this one. Together they ask whether memory keeps a city or quietly replaces it.`},{id:`desire`,name:`Cities & Desire`,index:1,color:`#d9776b`,blurb:`In these five cities desire is the hidden architect: it opens every road on a single bright morning, gilds the stones its cutters polish, turns one skyline into the ship or the camel of escape, shelves abandoned futures under glass, and lays out streets as a snare for a dream that never returns.`},{id:`signs`,name:`Cities & Signs`,index:2,color:`#c9b27c`,blurb:`Five cities that must be read before they can be seen: one buried under its own emblems, one that repeats itself into memory, one with no differences left to read, one whose signs point where you would never look, and one that can only be told truly in words that seem to lie. Together they ask whether a city is ever more than the signs we make of it.`},{id:`thin`,name:`Thin Cities`,index:3,color:`#9cc3c9`,blurb:`The Thin Cities are cities pared down to their armature, made of shafts, stilts, pipes, girders and ropes rather than walls, holding themselves at a distance from the ground. Across the five, lightness is both a way of building and a way of living, and each city asks how little it can keep and still remain a city.`},{id:`trading`,name:`Trading Cities`,index:4,color:`#e0a04a`,blurb:`In the Trading Cities, exchange outgrows the bazaar: memories are bartered by the fire, glances pass between strangers, citizens swap entire lives, bonds are strung from house to house, and routes are traded for routes. Each city asks whether its traders go home changed, or merely exchanged.`},{id:`eyes`,name:`Cities & Eyes`,index:5,color:`#7fb7a4`,blurb:`Cities that depend on who is looking: doubled in a lake, read up or down, watched from above the clouds, worn away by habit, or seen from their hidden back.`},{id:`names`,name:`Cities & Names`,index:6,color:`#b49ad1`,blurb:`In these five cities a name and a place slip out of register: the name builds a sturdier city than the stones, is claimed by rival household gods, is overwritten the moment you arrive, outlives every ruin, or holds true only from far away. Each diorama sets the word and the city side by side and lets you watch the gap between them.`},{id:`dead`,name:`Cities & the Dead`,index:7,color:`#a9a39a`,blurb:`In these five cities the dead are never quite elsewhere: they pass their roles to actors who will not live to see the play end, lend their faces to strangers on a quay, set fashions from a buried twin, lie still in a city whose air has turned to earth, and wait with the unborn in the two bulbs of an hourglass that no one turns. Together the cities ask how much of every living place is on loan from those who came before and those still waiting to arrive.`},{id:`sky`,name:`Cities & the Sky`,index:8,color:`#7d9be0`,blurb:`Cities that answer to the heavens: woven into a carpet, haunted by a golden double, built after a blueprint of stars, and mistaken in their astronomy.`},{id:`continuous`,name:`Continuous Cities`,index:9,color:`#9c8f86`,blurb:`Cities without edges, where waste, sameness, crowds and suburbs spread until the city covers the whole world.`},{id:`hidden`,name:`Hidden Cities`,index:10,color:`#8fbf6a`,blurb:`Cities concealed inside other cities: a pinpoint that grows, a thread of joy, a flight of swallows, the return of fabulous beasts, the just inside the unjust.`}],t=Object.fromEntries(e.map(e=>[e.id,e]));export{t as n,e as t};